Subject: keep the guest owner on link2symlink hard links

A fake hard link made by --link2symlink is a symlink to a hidden ".l2s.NAME"
file in the same directory. When the guest stats it, the link2symlink
extension answers with the backing file's stat -- it has to, for the type,
the link count and the inode -- and, outside the USERLAND build, wrote that
whole stat, owner included, over the buffer the kernel filled in. The
backing file is owned by the app like every other file of the guest, and
fake_id0 maps "owned by the app's uid" to the guest's uid (0 for --root-id)
on stat results. When fake_id0's handler ran before this one, the mapped
owner was overwritten with the raw host owner: the guest then saw the app's
uid (10727 on the test phone) on fake hard links through lstat, stat, fstat
and fstatat, while statx and ordinary files showed 0.

Observed by pacman -Qkk (libalpm compares the mtree's uid/gid with lstat):
every file that a package installs as a hard link (1093 of tzdata's 1887,
46 of coreutils', 14 of pacman's) reported "UID mismatch" and "GID mismatch";
bsdtar and find(1) show the same numbers. Contents and modes were never
affected.

The owner is now taken from the buffer as it stands -- mapped already, or
raw and mapped afterwards by fake_id0 -- so the result is the same in either
order. Everything else the extension fixes (type, mode bits, link count,
inode, size) is unchanged, and the USERLAND build keeps its own handling.
tests/garden-common/proot/owner-check.sh makes fake hard links, symlinks and
ordinary files and reads their owner through every stat flavour and find(1),
as root and as a fake non-root id.

Upstream: termux/proot @ 7266fb3e8516535682f5a9c8f3a7e70f6506eddb (v5.1.107.92), after patches 0001-0007

diff -ruN a/src/extension/link2symlink/link2symlink.c b/src/extension/link2symlink/link2symlink.c
--- a/src/extension/link2symlink/link2symlink.c
+++ b/src/extension/link2symlink/link2symlink.c
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #include "execve/execve.h"
 #include "path/f2fs-bug.h"
 #include "arch.h"
+#include "tracee/abi.h"
 #include "attribute.h"
 
 #ifdef USERLAND
@@ -975,6 +976,24 @@
 		else
 			sysarg_stat = SYSARG_2;
 
+		#ifndef USERLAND
+			/* The owner is whatever the tracee's stat buffer says now, not the
+			 * backing file's host owner: fake_id0 (which runs before or after
+			 * this handler, depending on how the syscall was reached) has
+			 * mapped, or will map, the app's uid and gid to the guest's, and
+			 * the file standing in for the hard link is owned by the app like
+			 * every other file. Writing the backing file's host owner over
+			 * the mapped one made a link look owned by the app's uid.  */
+			{
+				word_t buffer = peek_reg(tracee, ORIGINAL, sysarg_stat);
+				uint32_t current_uid = peek_uint32(tracee, buffer + offsetof_stat_uid(tracee));
+				if (errno == 0)
+					finalStat.st_uid = current_uid;
+				uint32_t current_gid = peek_uint32(tracee, buffer + offsetof_stat_gid(tracee));
+				if (errno == 0)
+					finalStat.st_gid = current_gid;
+			}
+		#endif
 		#ifdef USERLAND
 			/* Overwrite the stat struct with the correct number of "links". */
 			read_data(tracee, &statl, peek_reg(tracee, ORIGINAL, sysarg_stat), sizeof(statl));
